    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-20T09:17:49+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-20T09:17:49+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T23:47:49Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-19T23:47:49Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front will cross the west of the state this morning and will track across the east of the state during the day. Another high pressure system will move eastwards across waters to the south during Monday then over Victoria and the Tasman Sea on Tuesday. This high will extend a ridge westwards over SA ahead of a low pressure trough that is expected to move over the far west of SA during Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northwesterly 25 to 40 km/h shifting southerly 25 to 35 km/h in the afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures 27 to 36.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 3:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Marla in the afternoon and evening. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h turning southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h early in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then tending east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 26 to 31.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-24T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-23T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
